.claude/skills/integration-pr/reference/templates.md:56:.github/pull_request_template.md, every box left unticked}
.claude/skills/integration-pr/reference/templates.md:82:Pokedex CI reads the `test override:` line; the comment is for the human editing it. Write the `-k {name}` override yourself rather than leaving the template's `yarn test -s`, which only asks CI to pick the args from the diff (`.claude/rules/pull-requests.md` "CI test scope"). Copy the ship block from the repo template and leave every box unticked (`.claude/rules/pull-requests.md` "Ship on merge"). Refresh mode keeps this block verbatim, and appends it if it is missing.
.claude/skills/integration-pr/reference/templates.md:139:| `shipping_address.line1` | `shipTo.street` | |
.claude/skills/integration-pr/workflows/create.md:57:Keep each section short, as templates.md says below the template. Copy the CI override block and the ship block exactly where and as the template shows them, with `{name}` replaced.
.claude/skills/integration-pr/workflows/create.md:129:The `[TRA-XXXX]` prefix links the PR in Linear. If step 4 found no ticket, use a descriptive title without the prefix and say so in the Summary.
.claude/skills/integration-pr/workflows/create.md:137:1. Find the canonical resource. `get_orders` → `resources/{type}/orders.py`, using the integration's family (`wms` / `cart` / `carrier`). The `Order` / `Product` / `InboundShipment` / etc. class there holds the field list.
.claude/skills/integration-pr/workflows/create.md:173:- Reference artifacts, as step 5 left them: "gotchas + api-summary included" / "gotchas only" / "api-summary only" / "none surfaced" / "<filename> uncommitted, not shipped per user choice".

